{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch73TDNBYoVnvoET1oZ3L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I didn't use \"we cut picking errors in half.\" Only one of your six customers saw that drop. The one other customer with numbers went from 2.8 to 2.2, about 21%. If Dana asks for references, or her team checks your other customers, \"half\" will look like an overstatement and could cost you the deal. The email gives the pet-supply result as a single customer's numbers. That reads as a real result, and anyone who checks will find it's true.\n\nOther choices I made:\n\n- **Her $600K quote opens the email.** It shows you did your homework, and it's her number, not yours. I didn't project her savings because a figure built from one customer is easy to pick apart. Your annual price across five sites is $75,000, and I put it next to her $600K so she can make that comparison herself.\n- **The IT concern is handled without naming him.** One sentence says it sits on top of her warehouse system and doesn't replace it. That answers his likely objection before she forwards the email. I didn't claim it never touches their system, because your facts don't say that. If it's true, adding it would help.\n- **I didn't name the pet-supply customer**, since I don't know if they've agreed to be a reference. If they have, using their name makes the email stronger.\n- **Placeholders to fill in:** [Product], [Magazine], [Your name], [Company].\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Your $600K in wrong-item returns\n\nHi Dana,\n\nLast spring you told [Magazine] that returns from wrong-item shipments cost your company north of $600,000 a year. That's the problem we work on.\n\nWith [Product], pickers scan each item with a phone camera. If it's the wrong item, they find out before the box closes. At a regional pet-supply distributor with 3 warehouses, mis-picks fell from 4.1 to 1.9 per 1,000 order lines over their first five months.\n\nIt doesn't replace your warehouse management system. It runs on top of it. Setup takes about three weeks. It costs $1,250 per site per month, so $75,000 a year for all five of your warehouses.\n\nWould you be open to a 20-minute call to see whether those numbers could hold up in your buildings?\n\n[Your name]\nCo-founder, [Company]\n</final_document>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5498,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5498},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c58184bd-d049-4e9b-a716-ff56f23ca3f5","uuid":"b7acefeb-ec7b-4fe5-9f4a-1868f0196613","timestamp":"2026-11-16T18:00:19.655Z","request_id":"req_011Ch73TDA3DfaUcSUp3hZh4"}
